From f65ca629e4b1f8b278517ad815adab8251ce0f23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:40:55 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] CI: affected-test selection follows import-time
 imports; full suite runs 12 slices

Pull request CI took 14 min at p50 (p90 15.4, 60 green runs on 2026-11-18), nearly all of it the
eight Python slices at 10-11 min each. Two causes:

1. scripts/ci/affected_tests.py almost never selected. It followed function-level imports at every
   depth, which ties the source tree into one cycle: 80% of source modules reached 96% of the test
   files, over the 40% full-suite cutoff, so 54 of 60 pull requests ran the full suite ("9690 of
   10047 test files affected" for a 3-file change). Now a file under tests/ counts for every import
   it holds; a source module passes a change on through import-time imports only, except that a
   source module naming the changed module in a function-level import is itself affected (one hop).
   `if TYPE_CHECKING:` imports never count. Replaying the last 80 merged pull requests on this tree:
   69 select affected files (median 9% of the suite, p90 31%), 11 still run the full suite.
   Given up: a test that reaches the change only through a function-level import two or more source
   modules away runs on the main push, not on the pull request.

2. The suite grew from ~7.2 h to ~12.9 h of per-file time since the eight slices were sized
   (2026-10-29). MAX_SLICES and the tests.yml default go to 12 (~65 min of files, ~7-8 min a slice);
   SLICE_SECONDS drops to 16 x 240 so an affected slice is no larger than a full-suite one.
   upstream-sync.yml passes its own eight-slice list and its required job names, unchanged.

Proof: tests/ci/test_affected_tests.py 44 passed (new cases: import-time closure through a class body,
async def, one function-level hop and no second, TYPE_CHECKING bare and negated, a lazily importing hub), tests/ci/test_fast_runner_routing.py 19 passed,
tests/ci/test_detect_planner_checkout.py 2 passed, run with hermes-core-wt test --local on macOS;
ruff clean. Not run here: scripts/check and the Linux suite.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
